kind how-do-i
title How do I put back the vtium.conf I had before an install?
intro Each install keeps the vtium.conf it replaces. The Flow tab's o lists those files, newest first, and copies the one you choose into the draft, ready to install again.
see install-and-restore/save-on-quit-and-install-from-the-command-line

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Run `vtium-config set font-name mono`.
2. Run `vtium-config install`.
at the install
check installed has "font-name = mono"
3. Go to the Flow tab.
4. Press o to restore.
5. Press Enter to restore.
note vtium-config asks before it replaces the draft.
6. Press y for yes.
at the restore
check draft has "font-name = unifont"
